{
  "protocolVersion": "1.6.0",
  "spec": "https://github.com/tokensafe-dev/oumv/blob/main/spec/SPEC.md",
  "description": "Language-neutral OUMV conformance cases (spec §10). Each case declares the conformance Level (1|2|3) it certifies. A runtime attains Level N only when every case with level <= N passes; a failure at a higher level caps the claim but does not fail the lower levels. fixtureVersion 3 added session handshake, getSource and verify-result shape coverage; fixtureVersion 4 requires the observe `format` field the spec envelope mandates; fixtureVersion 5 covers applyEdit mode=create (new file, no overwrite). Markers substituted by each runner: ${FIXTURE_FILE}, ${MISSING_FILE}, ${EDIT_TARGET_FILE}, ${EDIT_TARGET_VERSION}, ${EDIT_CONTENT}, ${BROKEN_CONTENT}, ${L2_TARGET}, ${L3_TARGET}, ${VERIFY_TARGET}. v7 (wire 1.3.0): applyEdit mode=patch (splice, target-missing), getSource window/dedup markers, unknown mode/symbol/level/version, create with expectedVersion, rename/delete validation. v8: pushCases for the SSE (§2.3) and WebSocket (§2.4) bindings — a certificate for that transport proves a mutation is pushed as `state`/`notifications/oumv.state` and that `Last-Event-ID` replays it. v9: capabilityCases gated on the handshake claim (verify.sandboxRollback), markers are substituted in nested params, and a case a runtime does not claim is absent from its report rather than skipped. v10 (wire 1.5.0): the applyEdit batch envelope (mutate.multiFile) — one atomic call creates two files, and a batch whose second edit fails syntax pre-flight leaves no bytes on disk; sessionCases issue a handshake with `sessionTtlSeconds` and prove an expired id answers -32011 with data.reason=session_expired. v11 (wire 1.6.0): capabilityCases for the new optional surface — previewEdit never writes (a follow-up getSource with ifVersion proves the bytes untouched), the idempotency key replays the first create instead of answering file_exists, cancel of an unknown requestId is a result not an error, index returns the ranked-matches contract, query proves the read-only split (SELECT answers columns/rows, INSERT is -32003 query_forbidden) and build returns status/command/diagnostics. Gated on the handshake claim (mutate.preview, sessions.idempotency, sessions.cancel, index.symbols, observeQuery.readOnly, verify.build) — a runtime that does not advertise stays absent from the report. v12: the §4.1 result-versioning handshake as ordered cases gated by `minWireVersion` — observe and understand carry a `workspaceVersion` token, a matching `ifVersion` answers the short unchanged envelope, and a stale token is rejected with -32010 STALE_RESOURCE_VERSION (runtimes frozen on wire 1.5.0 skip these cases and are absent from their report).",
